  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pt3P!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd85d1c5-f421-4b5d-8d0c-333f69f3fa66_5741x3828.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pt3P!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd85d1c5-f421-4b5d-8d0c-333f69f3fa66_5741x3828.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"971\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><figcaption>Christopher Nolan attends the Mumbai premiere of “The Odyssey” on July 11, 2026. (Photo by <a href=\"https://www.gettyimages.com/search/2/image?artistexact=Aalok%20Soni\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Aalok Soni</a><span>/Stringer via Getty Images)</span></figcaption></figure>\n<p><span>I read “The Odyssey”</span><em></em><span>as a sophomore in high school — </span><em><span>read </span></em><span>is probably a strong word for what was realistically a skim. Regardless, once Odysseus returned home, I closed my </span><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0140268863?lv=shuf&amp;channelId=500&amp;plpRedirect=mhFallback\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Fagles</span></a><span> and never looked back. My young mind’s attention…</span></p>\n<p>\n          <a href=\"https://www.slowboring.com/p/thank-you-christopher-nolan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
